WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.275
So, four asks.

2
00:00:01.275 --> 00:00:05.824
Adopt the library: the Federal
Modernization Workbook's Book 04's

3
00:00:05.824 --> 00:00:10.963
Conditional Access library and wave
plan as the agency's access baseline.

4
00:00:10.963 --> 00:00:15.312
End standing privilege: every
administrator role eligible through PIM,

5
00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:19.588
with two governed break-glass accounts
as the only standing exception.

6
00:00:19.588 --> 00:00:22.785
Separate deciding from
executing: name the owners,

7
00:00:22.785 --> 00:00:27.124
scope the help desk role, and stand
up the identity governance office.

8
00:00:27.124 --> 00:00:30.048
And manage access as
code: version control,

9
00:00:30.048 --> 00:00:34.475
review and drift monitoring, with
the evidence kept from day one.

10
00:00:34.475 --> 00:00:38.775
In Zero Trust, every access
decision is a policy decision.

11
00:00:38.775 --> 00:00:41.244
Writing that policy down, testing it,

12
00:00:41.244 --> 00:00:45.687
and proving it ran is how an agency
knows who can reach what, and why.

13
00:00:45.687 --> 00:00:51.488
Book 04 has the full library and settings,
with every external claim footnoted.

14
00:00:51.488 --> 00:00:56.087
Book 05 covers the device compliance
that Conditional Access reads.

15
00:00:56.087 --> 00:00:56.900
Thank you.
